  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": null,
    "grammar": "Getting out of a place takes **from** (*escape from prison*); avoiding harm takes a direct object (*escape injury*). The sense *her name escapes me* has the thing forgotten as the subject and the person as the object.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "\"escape\" begins with a short vowel, *ih-SKAPE* or *eh-SKAPE*, with the stress on the second part. Do not start with *ex-*: there is no **k** sound before the **s**."
  },
